  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9266273b8f123004195741f969177dda, type: 3}
  title: The art folders
  sections:
  - heading: How do I organize art folders ?
    text: Art folders should be organized by topic rather than by asset type. Prefer
      "Environment", "Characters", "VFX" over "Meshes", "Materials" or "Shaders".
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Why should I do that ?
    text: Well because if you're looking for a specific asset type, you can use the
      search filters to find it. If you look for a rock, Unity won't tell it apart
      from a tree. Both are meshes, that's all it knows. Moreover, when working on
      a specific asset or task, it's convenient to have all the files related to
      this asset easily accessible in one place.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: What if I still have many materials hanging next to many meshes ?
    text: Once you've clearly separated assets from one another, you can start subdividing
      by asset type. For example, in your "Rocks" folder, you can have a "Big rocks"
      folder, that contains "Big rock 01", "Big rock 02" etc., which in turn contain
      "Meshes", "Materials", "Textures" folders.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
